# The freeze gate (decisions 0128, 0129, 0133): git runs this hook on every ref
# transaction, whatever route moves a branch (a commit, `--no-verify` included,
# an amend, a merge, a cherry-pick, a rebase, `update-ref`, a push into this
# repository), in every work tree of the repository. In the prepared state, an
# update of a branch that changes or deletes a journal entry is refused, as is
# one that brings in a change to what a cut not integrated freezes (its
# examples, held-out example text, frozen checks, the files they use, or a
# journal entry superseding or retiring a concept it realizes) unless
# `CRATYLUS_AGENT` names the cut's architect; the branch stays where it was.
# It is `cratylus freeze-gate`, run from this checkout's source (`tsx`), as the
# immutability gate is, so it needs no build. It runs where git runs the hook
# (a linked work tree's top, or the git directory on a push), so it reads the
# update from there; `prepare` names the hooks folder absolutely so git finds
# it from each. Other states and transactions touching no branch never start
# it; its stdin is always read. A gate that cannot start refuses.
updates=$(cat)
[ "$1" = prepared ] || exit 0
case "$updates" in
*" refs/heads/"*) ;;
*) exit 0 ;;
esac
root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
printf '%s\n' "$updates" | "$root/packages/runtime/node_modules/.bin/tsx" "$root/packages/runtime/src/freeze-gate/index.ts" "$@"
